 # JSON utility
 
-Run `python cli.py` with JSON on stdin. The identity action returns its value unchanged.
+Run `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin; one JSON result is printed on stdout.
+
+## Actions
+
+- `identity`: `{"action": "identity", "value": <any JSON value>}` returns `value` unchanged.
+- `evaluate`: `{"action": "evaluate", "coefficients": [c0, c1, ...], "x": <int>}` returns
+  `{"value": p(x), "derivative": p'(x)}` where `p(t) = c0 + c1*t + c2*t^2 + ...` with
+  coefficients in ascending power order. An empty `coefficients` list is the zero
+  polynomial (value 0, derivative 0). All arithmetic is exact Python integers, so
+  large results (up to 30 coefficients and |x| = 100) are never rounded.
+
+## CLI example
+
+```
+$ echo '{"action": "evaluate", "coefficients": [1, 2, 3], "x": 10}' | python cli.py
+{"value": 321, "derivative": 62}
+```
+
+## Boundary and error semantics
+
+- Boundaries: empty coefficients, single-coefficient constants (derivative 0), and
+  30 coefficients with values and `x` in -100..100 are all handled exactly.
+- Unknown actions raise `ValueError`; the CLI prints the error message on stderr,
+  prints nothing on stdout, and exits with status 2 (no traceback).
+- Input payloads are never mutated, even on failure; operations are atomic.
